01:04:37.410 --> 01:04:38.250
Down those stairs.

01:04:39.720 --> 01:04:41.000
It was her own idea to come here.

01:04:41.330 --> 01:04:41.690
Yes.

01:04:42.150 --> 01:04:44.500
Now, look, the first thing you do tomorrow morning

01:04:44.500 --> 01:04:46.180
is to call up her theater ticket agency.

01:04:46.660 --> 01:04:48.900
Get two seats for a couple of shows next week.

01:04:49.100 --> 01:04:50.060
Who for? Weekends?

01:04:50.260 --> 01:04:50.480
For her.

01:04:51.510 --> 01:04:52.570
Better make it four seats.

01:04:52.650 --> 01:04:53.710
And ask Junior and me.

01:04:54.170 --> 01:04:56.030
I'll get Junior to plan dinner first

01:04:56.030 --> 01:04:57.450
or a supper party afterwards.

01:04:58.240 --> 01:04:59.920
And then we'll all be brokenhearted.

01:05:00.120 --> 01:05:00.460
Take care.

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:00.180
Thank you.

01:10:32.250 --> 01:10:32.350
Thank you.

01:12:00.480 --> 01:12:01.850
Good morning. Ready?

01:12:02.740 --> 01:12:04.080
Ready? For what?

01:12:04.470 --> 01:12:05.890
To go to the summer house the way you planned.

01:12:07.740 --> 01:12:08.520
You're not dressed yet.

01:12:08.780 --> 01:12:09.660
But I told you.

01:12:10.730 --> 01:12:11.610
Oh, I am sorry.

01:12:12.330 --> 01:12:13.550
It must have been Anne I told.

01:12:15.900 --> 01:12:16.320
Told what?

01:12:17.350 --> 01:12:18.250
About the Rolstons.

01:12:19.000 --> 01:12:21.360
You see, yesterday was her birthday and tomorrow's mine.

01:12:21.750 --> 01:12:23.490
And every year she gives this birthday party.

01:12:23.870 --> 01:12:26.130
The day in between, I'd completely forgotten about it.

01:12:27.380 --> 01:12:27.880
What are you saying?

01:12:29.000 --> 01:12:29.960
That we're not going to the...

01:12:30.530 --> 01:12:32.230
We're going to the Ralston's instead.

01:12:33.420 --> 01:12:34.100
But you promised.

01:12:34.450 --> 01:12:37.950
I know, but I promised Eve first a long time ago.

01:12:38.890 --> 01:12:42.200
Listen, you said we were going to the summer house. You can't back out now.

01:12:42.540 --> 01:12:44.260
Lester, why are you so excited?

01:12:46.780 --> 01:12:53.350
I guess I was just disappointed. I mean, I've been looking forward to being alone with you. Another honeymoon.

01:12:55.040 --> 01:12:57.330
We can still have it next week.

01:12:57.520 --> 01:12:59.980
But you need a rest now. Why give it up for a dinner party?

01:13:00.060 --> 01:13:01.300
Oh, I'm feeling much better now.

01:13:01.540 --> 01:13:04.260
And besides, Steve and Junior will be back from Sacramento.

01:13:04.440 --> 01:13:08.780
I thought they weren't due until Monday.

01:13:09.380 --> 01:13:12.870
At the office. They'll be home tonight. She's asked them too.

01:13:13.650 --> 01:13:14.590
Dinner and bridge.

01:13:17.130 --> 01:13:18.110
Dinner and bridge.

01:13:18.230 --> 01:13:25.680
You might have told me sooner.

01:13:27.180 --> 01:13:28.080
Is it so important?

01:13:30.730 --> 01:13:35.230
No, I broke a golf date this afternoon.

01:13:36.250 --> 01:13:37.630
But you can still go out, it's early.

01:13:38.740 --> 01:13:39.320
Don't be cross.

01:13:41.380 --> 01:13:45.360
No, it's sweet of you to be disappointed.

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:01.460
Let's go to the club and see if I can get a game.

01:14:05.430 --> 01:14:07.460
Oh, don't be late.

01:14:08.730 --> 01:14:10.510
I've asked Steve, Irene and Junior for cocktails

01:14:10.510 --> 01:14:11.930
so we can all go on to Eve's together.

01:14:33.160 --> 01:14:40.060
with you let me cut it out i couldn't make her go could i couldn't carry her there you may have to

01:14:40.180 --> 01:14:45.630
there are only a few hours left this is our last chance our last chance i could have strangled her

01:14:45.630 --> 01:14:49.660
when she said we weren't going two old days thrown away lost we could have planned something

01:14:49.660 --> 01:14:59.100
could have worked it all out all right we can't waste any more time that's it hello

01:15:07.800 --> 01:15:09.950
Lester, it's got to be tonight.

01:15:11.350 --> 01:15:13.130
We can't take any chances and lose everything.

01:15:13.350 --> 01:15:15.290
It's got to be an accident, a quick accident.

01:15:16.640 --> 01:15:17.820
What kind of an accident?

01:15:20.020 --> 01:15:20.940
Kind, what kind?

01:15:21.080 --> 01:15:22.120
Oh, keep your voice down.

01:15:23.410 --> 01:15:24.730
Kind of an accident.

01:15:27.060 --> 01:15:28.300
Lester? Yeah.

01:15:30.190 --> 01:15:32.930
Remember that woman who tried to kill herself on Far Island?

01:15:33.540 --> 01:15:33.880
So?

01:15:34.500 --> 01:15:36.740
I took it away from her. Remember?

01:15:37.490 --> 01:15:37.870
What?

01:15:38.030 --> 01:15:40.480
What she tried to kill herself with.

01:15:40.620 --> 01:15:41.760
Well, what good does that do us?

01:15:42.570 --> 01:15:44.250
I've got it. I saved it.

01:15:45.310 --> 01:15:45.790
Show you.

01:16:00.030 --> 01:16:00.810
Breeze pills, everybody?

01:16:01.050 --> 01:16:01.650
Yes, sir.

01:16:01.750 --> 01:16:03.090
Always rum for one more.

01:16:03.350 --> 01:16:04.490
Oh, junior, please.

01:16:05.270 --> 01:16:07.770
Irene, I'm sorry I didn't know you were going to wear white tonight.

01:16:08.070 --> 01:16:11.070
If it's going to be embarrassing for you, I can run upstairs and change in a second.

01:16:11.310 --> 01:16:11.870
Oh, no.

01:16:12.090 --> 01:16:13.470
You look so lovely, Myra.

01:16:14.000 --> 01:16:14.420
Thank you.

01:16:14.720 --> 01:16:15.880
Hi, this is a wonderful martini.

01:16:16.240 --> 01:16:16.540
Thank you.

01:16:16.660 --> 01:16:17.420
The servants are off tonight.

01:16:17.600 --> 01:16:18.820
Excuse me while I get the hors d'oeuvre.

01:16:19.000 --> 01:16:20.600
Why don't we just stay here tonight?

01:16:22.170 --> 01:16:23.610
This is more fun than playing bridge.

01:16:25.060 --> 01:16:26.260
Bridge is a wonderful game.

01:16:26.730 --> 01:16:29.970
Occupies the mind, keeps you away from bad company, and...

01:16:30.120 --> 01:16:32.080
Heals a small but steady income.

01:16:32.430 --> 01:16:34.690
Well, if I must play bridge, I hope Myra's my partner.

01:16:35.420 --> 01:16:38.910
Okay, partner? Myra's mine is someplace else tonight.

01:16:39.240 --> 01:16:40.100
Come to the party, dear.

01:16:40.340 --> 01:16:41.380
Oh, I'm so sorry.

01:16:41.910 --> 01:16:43.990
I hate to break this up, but we're due at the Ralston's.

01:16:46.680 --> 01:16:47.840
I'll get my coat right away.

01:18:39.690 --> 01:18:43.530
A day ago tonight at the Rolfsons, Junior and I made seven spades, doubled and redoubled.

01:18:43.790 --> 01:18:45.820
Ready, everybody? I wasn't allowed.

01:18:46.260 --> 01:18:52.470
You all right? I think so.

01:18:52.590 --> 01:18:54.600
Get some water, somebody. How did it happen?

01:18:54.740 --> 01:18:56.320
Oh, I tripped over my coat.

01:18:56.820 --> 01:18:58.920
You're hailed as a ghost. I'm still alive.

01:18:59.140 --> 01:18:59.860
Sit on this chair here.

01:19:00.700 --> 01:19:01.580
Oh, my ankle.

01:19:01.740 --> 01:19:02.440
Which one is it?

01:19:02.600 --> 01:19:03.220
Let's have a look at it.

01:19:03.700 --> 01:19:06.940
This one, careful.

01:19:09.220 --> 01:19:10.060
Take the shoe off.

01:19:12.560 --> 01:19:14.110
Hey, that looks pretty bad.

01:19:14.210 --> 01:19:14.930
We'd better call the doctor.

01:19:15.210 --> 01:19:17.090
Oh, no, no, no, it isn't that serious.

01:19:17.780 --> 01:19:19.740
If it isn't better by tomorrow, I'll have it x-rayed.

01:19:20.150 --> 01:19:21.010
Here, drink this.

01:19:22.550 --> 01:19:22.950
Here, darling.

01:19:23.720 --> 01:19:24.120
Thank you.

01:19:29.600 --> 01:19:29.980
Try the stuff.

01:19:31.060 --> 01:19:32.320
No, I don't think you should.

01:19:32.840 --> 01:19:34.080
Exercise is good for it.

01:19:35.280 --> 01:19:35.720
Is it?

01:19:36.280 --> 01:19:37.680
Keeps the circulation going.

01:19:39.590 --> 01:19:41.580
All right, Irene. I'll try it.

01:19:43.220 --> 01:19:45.170
Lester, will you help?

01:19:45.550 --> 01:19:45.710
Sure.

01:19:52.780 --> 01:19:55.190
No, no, it's no use.

01:19:55.370 --> 01:19:57.050
I think you ought to get right to bed, Myra.

01:19:59.750 --> 01:19:59.890
Yes.

01:20:00.120 --> 01:20:01.000
Perhaps you're right.

01:20:02.260 --> 01:20:03.280
Maybe if you rested a while.

01:20:04.270 --> 01:20:05.310
Oh, no, I'm afraid not.

01:20:06.830 --> 01:20:09.530
I don't suppose there's any use asking you to go on without me.

01:20:09.840 --> 01:20:11.040
Not a husband like yours.

01:20:11.900 --> 01:20:13.420
I certainly wouldn't leave you alone.

01:20:15.920 --> 01:20:16.820
You'll have to go by yourselves.

01:20:18.110 --> 01:20:19.550
Tell even George how sorry we are.

01:20:19.910 --> 01:20:21.730
All right. I'll get your coat, Irene.

01:20:22.230 --> 01:20:24.430
The faster we get out of here, the sooner she'll get to bed.

01:20:25.150 --> 01:20:25.810
Sorry, Myra.

01:20:26.210 --> 01:20:28.920
I feel such a fool falling down the steps.

01:20:29.180 --> 01:20:29.960
So clumsy up.

01:20:30.350 --> 01:20:34.840
You insist on being your own doctor. Remember, it's ice packs for a sprain, not a hot water bottle.

01:20:34.960 --> 01:20:35.980
I know. Thank you, Steve.

01:20:36.360 --> 01:20:37.600
I'll take good care of you, Myra.

01:20:38.710 --> 01:20:39.430
Of course you will, Lester.

01:20:41.400 --> 01:20:42.660
I'll just put on my scarf.

01:20:43.160 --> 01:20:44.910
There's a mirror. Excuse me.

01:20:46.970 --> 01:20:48.930
I hope I haven't broken up your game tonight.

01:20:49.410 --> 01:20:50.930
Forget it. Just take care of your ankle.

01:20:51.180 --> 01:20:52.280
I will. Thank you, Junior.

01:21:00.420 --> 01:21:02.690
but I still think you ought to call the doctor.

01:21:04.600 --> 01:21:08.130
Please tell Eve how sorry I am. I know she'll understand.

01:21:08.270 --> 01:21:10.610
She'll understand, dear. Of course she will.

01:21:11.220 --> 01:21:12.880
I'll call after dinner to see how you feel.

01:21:13.250 --> 01:21:16.750
Yes, Steve. Good night.

01:21:17.890 --> 01:21:21.740
Good night. I do hope you feel better soon, Myra.

01:21:22.150 --> 01:21:22.790
Thank you, Irene.

01:21:27.500 --> 01:21:29.700
Please let yourselves out. I want to take Myra upstairs.

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:31.680
Good-bye. Good-night, Lester, Lyra.

01:21:32.160 --> 01:21:32.720
That's what you are.

01:22:03.200 --> 01:22:20.830
I'm sorry to spoil your evening, but you don't like bridge anyway.

01:22:26.470 --> 01:22:27.650
Would you get me an ice bag?

01:22:31.980 --> 01:22:33.280
And a cigarette, please.

01:22:51.970 --> 01:22:53.470
I'll see if there's an ice bag in the bathroom.

01:23:10.620 --> 01:23:12.540
No ice bag here. I'll have to go downstairs for one.

01:23:13.520 --> 01:23:15.420
Will you bring my coat? It's still on the stairs.

01:23:16.190 --> 01:23:19.980
Right. Ice bag, coat, and I'll pick up your shoe, too.

01:23:20.810 --> 01:23:23.820
Oh, and maybe a book. Would you like me to read to you after a while?

01:23:25.810 --> 01:23:28.540
Yes, I'd like that.

01:23:30.120 --> 01:23:31.380
I'd like that very much.

01:23:41.440 --> 01:23:42.880
Let mystery have its place in you.

01:23:44.530 --> 01:23:46.750
Do not be always turning up your whole soil

01:23:46.750 --> 01:23:48.990
with the plowshare of self-examination.

01:23:51.060 --> 01:23:52.760
Leave a little fallow corner in your heart

01:23:52.760 --> 01:23:54.680
ready for any seed the winds may bring

01:23:54.680 --> 01:23:57.920
and reserve a nook of shadow for the passing bird.

01:24:00.250 --> 01:24:02.110
a place in your heart for the unexpected guest,

01:24:03.660 --> 01:24:05.120
an altar for the unknown god.

01:24:06.760 --> 01:24:08.540
Then if a bird sing among your branches,

01:24:10.140 --> 01:24:11.660
do not be too eager to tame it.

01:24:13.600 --> 01:24:15.060
If you are conscious of something new,

01:24:16.180 --> 01:24:19.020
thought or feeling wakening in the depths of your being,

01:24:20.300 --> 01:24:22.120
do not be in a hurry to let in light upon it.

01:24:23.040 --> 01:24:26.540
Look at it. Let the springing germ

01:24:26.540 --> 01:24:29.620
have the protection of being forgotten.

01:24:32.010 --> 01:24:33.210
Edge it around with quiet.

01:24:35.790 --> 01:24:37.050
Do not break in upon its darkness.

01:24:40.470 --> 01:24:43.400
Let it take shape for all.

01:25:01.240 --> 01:25:01.640
Are you asleep?

01:26:40.010 --> 01:26:40.330
Thank you.

01:27:03.130 --> 01:27:03.150
Thank you.

01:29:34.120 --> 01:29:39.500
You have been found guilty of murder in the first degree, and for the killing of Lester Blaine, you will be sentenced to death.

01:30:02.780 --> 01:30:03.020
Thank you.

01:30:30.480 --> 01:30:30.520
Thank you.

01:32:50.190 --> 01:32:51.680
Let me go.

01:32:51.840 --> 01:32:53.040
How about buying you a little drink?

01:32:53.060 --> 01:32:53.860
Let me go, please.

01:32:53.900 --> 01:32:54.500
Oh, come on.

01:32:54.680 --> 01:32:55.980
I said let me go!

01:34:14.460 --> 01:34:17.100
Junior, it's nice of you to bring me home from the party so early

01:34:17.100 --> 01:34:18.780
when you were having such a good time.

01:34:28.220 --> 01:34:29.760
Please, Junior, I have a headache.

01:34:30.190 --> 01:34:31.870
I'm going to take an aspirin and go to bed.

01:34:32.150 --> 01:34:34.150
I've run into some stiff competition in my time.

01:34:34.710 --> 01:34:36.630
It's the first time I ever tangled with an aspirin.

01:34:37.150 --> 01:34:39.450
Junior, I told you why I came home early.

01:34:39.690 --> 01:34:41.430
I know. It's awfully good for a headache.

01:34:42.450 --> 01:34:44.430
Why don't you just relax and let yourself go?

01:34:44.630 --> 01:34:45.850
Not tonight, Junior. Please.

01:34:46.160 --> 01:34:47.520
Don't send me away. Not now.

01:34:48.120 --> 01:34:49.440
I don't want to. You know that.

01:34:49.780 --> 01:34:52.120
For this headache. That's why I left the party early.

01:34:52.360 --> 01:34:53.940
You're much too beautiful to have a headache.

01:35:01.980 --> 01:35:03.500
You needn't crush me to death.

01:35:03.950 --> 01:35:07.630
I'm sorry, it's just how I've been driving myself crazy imagining things.

01:35:08.540 --> 01:35:09.880
Imagining maybe there's someone else.

01:35:10.870 --> 01:35:12.170
When do you give me a chance?

01:35:12.430 --> 01:35:14.790
If there were, I'd kill him.

01:35:16.020 --> 01:35:17.160
You wouldn't kill anyone.

01:35:20.070 --> 01:35:20.430
I'm not.

01:35:22.940 --> 01:35:23.780
You're not the type.

01:35:33.100 --> 01:35:35.080
There now. Satisfied?

01:35:35.910 --> 01:35:38.490
The answer is no, but I'll go.

01:35:40.440 --> 01:35:41.120
Just one more?

01:35:42.180 --> 01:35:43.120
Good night, Junior.

01:35:44.680 --> 01:35:46.000
All right, but take care of yourself.

01:35:47.040 --> 01:35:47.540
See you tomorrow.

01:35:47.870 --> 01:35:48.150
Tomorrow.

01:38:23.708 --> 01:38:23.908
Oh.

01:42:22.720 --> 01:42:23.260
Green, where are you?

01:42:28.120 --> 01:42:28.940
Green, open the door!

01:42:37.770 --> 01:42:40.690
Irene? Irene, where are you?

01:44:23.160 --> 01:44:23.420
Help me.

01:47:01.950 --> 01:47:02.190
Thank you.

01:49:30.860 --> 01:49:32.480
What a smash-up.

01:49:33.460 --> 01:49:35.720
Don't touch anything. You gotta wait for the ambulance.

01:49:47.330 --> 01:49:47.970
The girl's dead, too.
